- during bilateral contraction, it extends the trunk;

- it stabilizes the twelfth rib during inspiration (Standring, 2016).

The genioglossus muscle is involved in multiple actions:

- during unilateral contraction, it laterally moves the tongue to the opposite side;

- during bilateral contraction, it protrudes the tongue and depresses the central portion of the tongue (Standring, 2016).

The orbicularis oculi muscle is a broad, flat muscle that encircles the orbit, thus forming a sphincter around each of the eye sockets. It may be divided into three portions:

- orbital part;

- palpebral part;

- lacrimal part.

The palpebral part originates from the medial palpebral ligament.

The orbicularis oculi muscle is a broad, flat muscle that encircles the orbit, thus forming a sphincter around each of the eye sockets. It may be divided into three portions:

- orbital part;

- palpebral part;

- lacrimal part.

The orbital part of the orbicularis oculi muscle originates from the nasal part of the frontal bone, the frontal process of maxilla, and the medial palpebral ligament.

The orbicularis oculi muscle is a broad, flat muscle that encircles the orbit, thus forming a sphincter around each of the eye sockets. It may be divided into three portions:

- orbital part;

- palpebral part;

- lacrimal part.

The lacrimal part arises from the posterior lacrimal crest of the lacrimal bone.

The platysma muscle is involved in multiple actions:

- tenses the skin of the neck;

- draws the lips and angles of the mouth downwards;

- assists in depression of the mandible at the temporomandibular joint (Standring, 2016).

The temporalis muscle is involved in multiple actions:

- elevates the mandible at the temporomandibular joint;

- retracts the mandible at the temporomandibular joint (Standring, 2016).

Overall, the masseter muscle is involved in multiple actions:

- elevates the mandible at the temporomandibular joint;

- assists in protraction of the mandible at the temporomandibular joint (Standring, 2016).

